00:13:48.360 --> 00:13:51.130
to avoid assembling or placing the object

274
00:13:51.130 --> 00:13:53.866
directly on hard surfaces to prevent damage.

275
00:13:54.166 --> 00:13:58.370
Recommends using a protective mat or rug underneath during assembly.

276
00:13:58.871 --> 00:14:02.575
That is basically a picture-perfect description of that picture.

277
00:14:03.108 --> 00:14:05.711
You can also see that the response for each figure

278
00:14:05.711 --> 00:14:09.215
is quite a bit longer than from dpt-2.

279
00:14:09.415 --> 00:14:13.986
For those of you analyzing things like marketing materials or magazines,

280
00:14:13.986 --> 00:14:16.388
You're going to encounter documents such as this,

281
00:14:16.488 --> 00:14:18.791
which are fundamentally infographics.

282
00:14:19.692 --> 00:14:22.695
This is really putting the layout detection through its paces,

283
00:14:22.795 --> 00:14:26.699
but the figure and text and logo and table chunks here

284
00:14:26.799 --> 00:14:28.801
actually look pretty solid.

285
00:14:29.168 --> 00:14:31.971
The only chunk type that we haven't seen so far

