00:14:43.682 --> 00:14:45.985
so let's take a look at how it's parsed.

291
00:14:46.485 --> 00:14:50.389
So here the turquoise is an attestation chunk type.

292
00:14:50.689 --> 00:14:52.791
And these are really difficult examples.

293
00:14:53.292 --> 00:14:56.595
Here we have curved text inside of the stamp

294
00:14:57.196 --> 00:14:59.365
with other text in the background and

295
00:14:59.365 --> 00:15:01.500
a separate signature off to the side.

296
00:15:01.901 --> 00:15:04.703
Let's take a look at the parse result for this chunk.

297
00:15:05.704 --> 00:15:08.407
So the content begins here with this attestation.

298
00:15:08.707 --> 00:15:12.711
So we're told that it's an official company stamp and signature.

299
00:15:12.912 --> 00:15:15.314
The signature itself is legible

300
00:15:15.314 --> 00:15:17.716
and is provided back to us in the markdown.

301
00:15:18.417 --> 00:15:20.552
As is the text from the

302
00:15:20.552 --> 00:15:23.022
stamp itself. There were two of these

303
00:15:23.022 --> 00:15:26.625
and you can see that the counterparty's signature is also legible

304
00:15:26.625 --> 00:15:28.427
as is the second stamp.

305
00:15:28.928 --> 00:15:30.829
That wraps up exercise two.

306
00:15:31.230 --> 00:15:35.034
In this section, you saw how the agentic approach to document extraction

307
00:15:35.034 --> 00:15:39.738
is able to handle complexity within a document and across documents

308
00:15:39.738 --> 00:15:43.442
without any additional actions or inputs from the users.

309
00:15:43.943 --> 00:15:46.245
This means that agentic document extraction

310
00:15:46.245 --> 00:15:49.415
can be used reliably in document processing pipelines

311
00:15:49.415 --> 00:15:53.018
that encounter such real-world complexity and variability.

